{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LTXyrTuSZUpineUjWnuMa3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information about CoRL 2026, though the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details are limited. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and is qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Reference to Previous Guidelines\n\nWhile specific 2026 reviewer guidelines were not found in the search results, the search did locate CoRL 2023 guidelines that emphasize being constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements.\n\nThe official CoRL 2026 submission and review materials are available through the OpenReview platform at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference. For the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form specifications for CoRL 2026, you may need to check that OpenReview link directly or contact the conference organizers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f420d955-7ae5-4224-93b3-f4bdf2a953a4","uuid":"0f762316-2805-45a8-af45-be63078a3681","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:02:28.965Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019fVQjb4Jk7ZCPGGepfnhQe","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some information about CoRL 2026, though the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details are limited. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and is qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Reference to Previous Guidelines\n\nWhile specific 2026 reviewer guidelines were not found in the search results, the search did locate CoRL 2023 guidelines that emphasize being constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements.\n\nThe official CoRL 2026 submission and review materials are available through the OpenReview platform at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference. For the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form specifications for CoRL 2026, you may need to check that OpenReview link directly or contact the conference organizers."],"durationSeconds":5.372644790999999}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQXEqfekU67eiGGeBcMyRv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 conference on robot learning reviewer guidelines scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"RULERS: Locked Rubrics and Evidence-Anchored Scoring for Robust LLM Evaluation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.08654\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, though the most detailed results are from CoRL 2023 and 2024 rather than specifically 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Reviewer Guidelines\n\nReviewers evaluate papers based on relevance to robot learning, including whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, evaluates the method in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in the paper.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers are asked to treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation.\n\nObvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in reviewer scores.\n\n## Reviewer Conduct Guidelines\n\nReviewers are instructed to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects, suggesting improvements, and accepting diverse views in discussions.\n\nUnfortunately, I was unable to find a specific detailed scoring rubric for CoRL 2025 in the search results. The CoRL 2025 conference has already concluded (it was held in Seoul, Korea), so specific reviewer materials from that year may not be publicly available or easily searchable. You may want to check the OpenReview platform directly or contact the CoRL organizers for access to the complete reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f420d955-7ae5-4224-93b3-f4bdf2a953a4","uuid":"fdf304b9-d821-41e6-9f56-e6b119335494","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:02:30.398Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 conference on robot learning reviewer guidelines scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013nBNJAdcZXXsK3aHcN7Wyv","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025","url":"https://2025.corl.org/"},{"title":"RULERS: Locked Rubrics and Evidence-Anchored Scoring for Robust LLM Evaluation","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.08654"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, though the most detailed results are from CoRL 2023 and 2024 rather than specifically 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Reviewer Guidelines\n\nReviewers evaluate papers based on relevance to robot learning, including whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, evaluates the method in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in the paper.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers are asked to treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation.\n\nObvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in reviewer scores.\n\n## Reviewer Conduct Guidelines\n\nReviewers are instructed to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects, suggesting improvements, and accepting diverse views in discussions.\n\nUnfortunately, I was unable to find a specific detailed scoring rubric for CoRL 2025 in the search results. The CoRL 2025 conference has already concluded (it was held in Seoul, Korea), so specific reviewer materials from that year may not be publicly available or easily searchable. You may want to check the OpenReview platform directly or contact the CoRL organizers for access to the complete reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric."],"durationSeconds":6.291190236999999}}
