{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016D6SQ99uGZoqY5MGQeaHW7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0194HGtGfnwzoV7Zk1AQYGPU","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a robotics/ML conference review (CoRL). Your focus areas are **Methods** and **Experiments**. \n\n## Venue Standards\nCoRL (Conference on Robot Learning). Acceptance rate ~36%. OpenReview 1-10 scale:\n- 10: Top 5%, seminal\n- 9: Top 15%, strong accept  \n- 8: Top 50%, clear accept\n- 7: Good paper, accept\n- 6: Marginally above threshold\n- 5: Marginally below threshold\n- 4: Not good enough, reject\n- 3: Clear rejection\n\nReview dimensions: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations.\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation: When 98% of Collision Avoidance is an Illusion\"\n\nThe paper studies Vision-Language-Action (VLA) model safety evaluation. Key claims:\n\n1. **Fake safety taxonomy**: The widely-used Collision Avoidance Rate (CAR) metric is systematically contaminated by two failure modes—action collapse (robot freezes, trivially safe) and geometric path safety (conservative motions that coincidentally avoid obstacles). Across Pi0 (170M), Pi0.5 (300M), and OpenVLA (7B), 92–99.6% of \"safe\" episodes are fake.\n\n2. **Displacement-filtered CAR (dfCAR)**: Proposed corrected metric: dfCAR = |{i: d_obs_i < ε ∧ d_ee_i > δ}| / N, using δ=0.1m threshold based on minimum displacement to complete SafeLIBERO tasks.\n\n3. **SDF auxiliary loss**: Training-time Signed Distance Field loss on Pi0.5 via LoRA produces real collision avoidance (+25pp filtered CAR, 0% fake safety), but devastates task performance (TSR: 73%→7%). 4-point λ curve shows dose-dependent relationship.\n\n4. **Two-phase training**: SDF pre-training (10K steps, λ=0.005) → standard fine-tuning (20K steps, λ=0) recovers TSR to 48% while retaining 81% safety encoding (CAR 45%, fake safe 5%).\n\n**Key experimental results** (from paper Tables 1-10):\n- Table 1: A1 (Pi0+LoRA+SDF) action collapse confirmed: 800ep obstacle disp median ~5nm, 50ep EE disp 96% < 1mm\n- Table 2: Cross-model comparison: Pi0 A1 (CAR 91.5%, fake 99.6%), Pi0.5 baseline (CAR 26.8%, fake 98.2%), OpenVLA (CAR 88%, fake 92%)\n- Table 3: OpenVLA per-task (4 tasks, 200ep total)\n- Table 4: LoRA attribution - LoRA-only CAR=27±1.4% ≈ zero-shot 26.8±1.6%, confirming SDF is the driver\n- Table 5: Per-task LoRA vs SDF showing asymmetry (milk +70pp, bbq_sauce -24pp)\n- Table 6: 4-point λ curve: λ∈{0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.1}, CAR monotonically increasing with diminishing returns\n- Table 7: Two-phase results: TSR=48%, CAR=45%, fake safe=5%\n- Table 8: Per-task Phase 2 breakdown, 76-100% safety retention\n- Table 9: Cross-scene (object_pudding vs spatial_bowl), both show +25-32pp CAR\n- Table 10: spatial_bowl per-task results\n\n**Experimental scale**: 70+ experiments, 6000+ episodes, 3 model families, 2 scenes, multiple seeds.\n\n## Experiment Design Context (from review_context.yaml)\nThe paper's imagined experiments include:\n- A1 EE Displacement Re-eval (50ep) — validates action collapse via EE metric\n- OpenVLA Zero-shot SafeLIBERO Eval (200ep) — cross-architecture validation\n- LoRA Baseline Eval (2 seeds) — attribution control\n- Phase 2 λ=0 Ablation Training (10K→30K) — two-phase strategy\n- Phase 2 λ=0 Eval (200ep) — key results\n- spatial_bowl A1 Eval (200ep) — cross-scene\n- Lambda=0.1 Bracket Training + Eval — dose-response curve\n\nNotable: The paper covers all planned experiments from the design. OpenVLA is zero-shot only (no fine-tuning). Phase 2 has only 1 seed. spatial_bowl has only 1 seed.\n\n## Your Task\nWrite a detailed review focusing on:\n\n### Methods Evaluation\n- Is dfCAR well-motivated and well-defined? Is δ=0.1m justified?\n- Is the SDF loss formulation sound? Any issues with EE-only supervision?\n- Is the two-phase training protocol well-designed? Are the phase durations justified?\n- Are there methodological gaps or confounds?\n\n### Experiments Evaluation  \n- Are experiments sufficient to support each claim?\n- Statistical rigor: seed counts, episode counts, confidence intervals\n- Are baselines adequate? Missing comparisons?\n- Cross-architecture claim (3 models) — is OpenVLA zero-shot a fair comparison?\n- Cross-scene claim (2 scenes) — sufficient for generalization?\n- Phase 2 single seed — is this a concern?\n- Any cherry-picking risks?\n\n### Output Format\nProvide your review in this structure:\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods & Experiments\n\n### Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths (bulleted)\n\n### Weaknesses (bulleted)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n\n### Missing Experiments or Controls\n\n### Scoring\n- Quality: X/10\n- Clarity: X/10\n- Significance: X/10\n- Relevance: X/10\n- Overall: X/10\n- Confidence: X/5 (1=low, 5=expert)\n```\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a CoRL-level review.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":58862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f420d955-7ae5-4224-93b3-f4bdf2a953a4","uuid":"e9df99c6-9d70-4eb2-a322-d7597e6d2f52"}
