{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G636EFCbJqHKrffVZKs7RL","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/diff_collision_sdf/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"CoRL 2026 / ICRA 2027\\\\\\\"\\\\n  track: main\\\\n  template: templates/latex/corl2026/\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"需确认 CoRL 2026 官方模板; fallback CoRL 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8\\\\n  deadline: 2026-06-13\\\\n  working_title: \\\\\\\"The Safety Illusion: How Action Collapse Contaminates Collision Avoidance Metrics in Vision-Language-Action Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    VLA safety 评估存在系统性缺陷：collision avoidance rate (CAR) 被 action collapse 严重污染。\\\\n    我们通过大规模实证分析（39 experiments, 5000+ episodes）揭示 fake safety 现象，\\\\n    提出 displacement-filtered CAR 作为修正指标，并展示 training-time SDF auxiliary supervision\\\\n    在能力充分的 VLA 上产生真实碰撞避免行为（pending Claim 4）。\\\\n  paper_type: analysis  # analysis paper with (pending) positive method contribution\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-24T14:00:00Z\\\\n  supersedes: \\\\\\\"ColliForce-VLA method paper (writing_plan v1, 2026-05-20)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 200\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"问题：VLA collision avoidance 中 CAR 被 action collapse 污染——高 CAR ≠ 真正碰撞避免\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"发现 1：91.5% CAR 中 99.6% 是 fake safe (robot displacement < 0.1mm)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"发现 2：TSR-CAR 反相关——能力越强的 VLA 碰撞越多 (Pi0.5 TSR=74.7% CAR=26.8%)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"发现 3：EE-only SDF 存在结构性缺陷——GT oracle 均劣于 baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"贡献：displacement-filtered CAR 指标 + [Claim 4 placeholder: SDF aux on Pi0.5]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [analysis_claim1, analysis_claim2, analysis_claim3, experimental_framework]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: VLA safety 是部署核心障碍; SafeLIBERO 系统量化碰撞问题; 多个方法报告高 CAR\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: 高 CAR 可能是 'safety illusion'——action collapse 让 robot 停止运动而非绕开障碍物\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 1: A1 SDF aux loss 报告 91.5% CAR, 但 99.6% 来自 displacement < 0.1mm 的 frozen episodes\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 2: Pi0.5 (TSR=74.7%) vs Pi0 (TSR≈0%): 能力越强→运动越多→碰撞越多. 'High CAR' on Pi0 = inability to move\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 3: 3 组 GT SDF oracle refinement 均劣于 baseline, fake_safe 仍 96-98%——EE-only SDF 结构性不足\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Solution: displacement-filtered CAR (CAR_f) 指标——仅计算 displacement > threshold 的 episode\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: [C1] fake safety phenomenon + CAR_f metric; [C2] capability-safety anti-correlation; [C3] EE-only structural limitation + oracle evidence; [C4 placeholder] SDF aux on capable VLA\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [analysis_claim1]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SafeLIBERO/AEGIS (Hu et al. 2025) — benchmark + existing safety method\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SafeVLA (Zhang et al. 2025) — RL-based safety\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"π0 (Black et al. 2024) — base architecture\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"CoFreeVLA (2026) — dual-arm safety\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 700\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§2.1 Collision-Safe VLA: AEGIS CBF post-hoc, SafeVLA CMDP, CoFreeVLA risk estimator, CAPE inference-time, iKinQP-RL QP correction, Li et al. cost-guided denoising → 共同点: 报告 CAR 但未检验 metric validity\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§2.2 SDF in Robotics: DeepSDF, iSDF, DiffCo, VoxPoser, SAMP → SDF 用于碰撞检测/规划, 我们揭示 EE-only SDF 在 VLA 中的结构性限制\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§2.3 Evaluation Reliability in Robot Learning: metric gaming / benchmark saturation 文献 → 我们将 metric contamination 问题带入 VLA safety 评估领域\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [introduction]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experimental_framework\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"Experimental Framework\\\\\\\"\\\\n    word_budget: 900\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.1 Benchmark & Models: SafeLIBERO object_pudding (4 tasks, Level I); Pi0 (openpi) + Pi0.5 基座; Full-FT / LoRA / A1-SDF 训练方案; evaluation protocol (50 ep/task)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.2 Standard Metrics: CAR (collision avoidance rate), TSR (task success rate) — 定义 + SafeLIBERO 原始公式\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.3 Displacement-Filtered CAR (CAR_f): 核心方法论贡献. 定义 action collapse (max displacement < τ_d=0.1mm). CAR_f = safe episodes with displacement ≥ τ_d / total non-collapsed episodes. Motivation: CAR 不区分 'safe because avoided' vs 'safe because frozen'\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.4 SDF Auxiliary Training (A1): SDF Decoder (4-layer MLP, ~395K params) + EE Extractor (2-layer MLP, ~263K params); SDF loss + EE loss as auxiliary objectives; LoRA fine-tuning on π0/π0.5. 为 Claims 1,3,4 提供实验方法\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.5 Oracle SDF Refinement: GT SDF gradient-based action refinement at inference (3 variants: adaptive α, fixed α, feature-space). 为 Claim 3 提供 upper bound 实验设计\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    notation_table:\\\\n      \\\\\\\"CAR\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Collision Avoidance Rate — fraction of episodes without collision\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"CAR_f\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Displacement-Filtered CAR — excludes action-collapsed episodes\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"TSR\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Task Success Rate\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"SSR\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Simultaneous Success Rate (TSR ∩ CAR)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"d_max(τ)\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Maximum EE displacement in episode τ\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"τ_d\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Displacement threshold = 0.1mm\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Φ(x)\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Signed distance at point x (>0 free, =0 surface, <0 penetration)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"f_SDF\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SDF Decoder — 4-layer MLP predicting workspace SDF from VLA features\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"f_EE\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"EE Extractor — 2-layer MLP predicting end-effector position\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\"λ_SDF\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SDF auxiliary loss weight\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: analysis_claim1\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"The Fake Safety Problem\\\\\\\"\\\\n    word_budget: 650\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.1 (or §5.1): Fake Safety is Pervasive\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"A1-LoRA (Pi0) 800ep: CAR=91.5%, 但 732 safe episodes 中 729 (99.6%) displacement < 0.1mm\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Displacement histogram: 73.9% < 1µm, 25.7% 1µm-0.1mm, 0.4% 0.1mm-1mm, 0% > 1mm\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"LoRA baseline 200ep: CAR=82%, fake_safe=99.4% — fake safety 不是 A1 特有, 是 action collapse 通病\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Pi0.5 baseline: safe episodes 中 98.2% 也是 fake (仅 s0 数据)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"displacement-filtered CAR: 所有 Pi0 方法 → CAR_f ≈ 0%; Pi0.5 baseline → CAR_f ≈ 0.5%\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Table 1 (tab1_fake_safety): 跨方法 fake safety 统计全景\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Fig 2 (fig2_displacement): displacement 分布直方图, 0.1mm 阈值标注\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experimental_framework]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary Table 2 + A1 displacement distribution\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: analysis_claim2\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"Capability-Safety Anti-correlation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    word_budget: 400\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.2 (or §5.2): More Capable Models Collide More\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Pi0.5 3-seed: TSR=74.7±1.5%, CAR=26.8±1.6% (n=600)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Pi0 baselines: TSR≈0%, CAR=82-83% — high CAR 来自 inability to move\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"TSR-CAR scatter plot (Fig 3): Pi0 系聚集左上角 (fake safety zone), Pi0.5 baseline 右下\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Framing: observation, not causal claim. 机制: 能力→运动→接近障碍物→碰撞\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Implication: CAR 单独不足以评估 safety, 必须与 TSR 联合解读\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [analysis_claim1]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary Table 4 scatter data\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: analysis_claim3\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"EE-Only SDF Structural Limitation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    word_budget: 600\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.3 (or §5.3): End-Effector-Only SDF Cannot Ensure Full-Body Safety\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3 oracle variants (all use GT SDF): adaptive CAR=75%, fixed CAR=73.1%, feature CAR=76.9%\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"所有 oracle 均 < baseline CAR=82%; fake_safe_rate 仍 96-98%\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"根因: SDF gradient 推 EE 远离障碍物, 但 arm body 可能被推向障碍物\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Feature-space oracle: 每步 241.7 refinements (vs action-space 14.2), gradient 幅度极小 (0.004-0.006), 效果无显著差异\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Per-task CAR 分解: task1 (chocolate_pudding) 是所有方法难点\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle bar chart (Fig 4): 3 variants + baselines, overlay fake_safe_rate\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Table 3 (tab3_oracle): 完整数据\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [analysis_claim1]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary Table 3 + per-task data\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: analysis_claim4_placeholder\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"[PLACEHOLDER] SDF Auxiliary Loss on Capable VLA\\\\\\\"\\\\n    word_budget: 250\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.4 (or §5.4): 10K Preview — First Evidence of Real Collision Avoidance\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Pi0.5+A1 s0: λ=0.005 CAR=58%, λ=0.01 CAR=56.5%; TSR=47-49%; frozen_rate=0%\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"与 baseline 对比: CAR +30pp, TSR -26pp, 0% frozen → first method with non-fake safety\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[TODO: 30K 3-seed × 2-lambda 完整结果]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[TODO: LoRA baseline 对比 — 归因 SDF vs LoRA capacity]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[TODO: Task-dependent tradeoff 分析 (Task 0-2 up, Task 3 down)]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [analysis_claim1, analysis_claim2, analysis_claim3]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"ROADMAP D016 + pending 30K eval\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion_placeholder\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"[PLACEHOLDER] Discussion & Conclusion\\\\\\\"\\\\n    word_budget: 300\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[PLACEHOLDER] 等 Claim 4 完整数据\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Summary: fake safety pervasive → CAR_f metric → EE-only limitation → [Claim 4]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Implications for VLA safety evaluation community\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitations: SafeLIBERO only, 2 model families (Pi0/Pi0.5), single task suite (object_pudding)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Future: full-body SDF, additional VLA architectures, real-robot validation, standardized safety benchmarks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [analysis_claim4_placeholder]\\\\n\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_concept\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: paperbanana\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Fake vs real safety 概念图 — 左: fake safe (frozen robot, misleading ✓), 右: real safe (robot navigating around obstacle, genuine ✓)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"一图说明核心概念: 高 CAR 不等于碰撞避免, displacement 才是区分 fake/real safety 的关键\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"两面板对比: 左=frozen robot + 'Safe ✓' label + 'displacement ≈ 0', 右=robot avoiding + 'Safe ✓' + 'displacement > τ'\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"左面板加红色警告: 'Action Collapse'\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"底部示意: standard CAR counts both → CAR_f filters left panel\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"简洁, 顶会品质, 不是 tutorial diagram\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: introduction\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:9\\\\\\\"\\\\n    priority: important\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig2_displacement\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Displacement 分布直方图 — A1-LoRA (800ep) + LoRA baseline (200ep), log-scale, 0.1mm threshold\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"99.6% safe episodes 的 displacement < 0.1mm → CAR 被 action collapse 严重污染\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Log-scale x-axis (displacement), count on y-axis\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Vertical dashed line at τ_d = 0.1mm with annotation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Left of threshold: red/pink fill (fake safe zone)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Right of threshold: green fill (real safe zone)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"A1 800ep 数据: <1µm: 541, 1µm-0.1mm: 188, 0.1mm-1mm: 3, >1mm: 0\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"可选: 叠加 Pi0.5 baseline 的 displacement 分布做对比\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"NO matplotlib defaults. 白背景, 精细字号, 专业配色\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary: A1-LoRA displacement bins\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: analysis_claim1\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    priority: must\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig3_tsr_car_scatter\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"TSR vs CAR scatter — 全方法对比, 区分 fake/real safe\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"Pi0 系方法聚集左上角 (fake safety zone); Pi0.5+A1 唯一向右上移动且 0% frozen\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"X=TSR [0,1], Y=CAR [0,1]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Shaded region upper-left: 'Fake Safety Zone' (high CAR, low TSR)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hollow markers: fake-safe-dominated methods (Pi0 系)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Filled markers: real-safe methods (Pi0.5+A1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Pi0.5 baseline: filled blue circles\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Annotate key clusters with method family names\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Star marker for Pi0.5+A1 (the promising direction)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Data from paper_data_summary Table 4\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary: Table 4 scatter data points\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: analysis_claim2\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"1:1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    priority: important\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig4_oracle_bar\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Oracle refinement CAR comparison — 3 GT SDF oracle variants + baselines\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"即使 GT SDF + oracle refinement 也无法提升 CAR 超过 baseline → EE-only 结构性缺陷\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Grouped bars: x=methods, y=CAR\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Baseline (gray): LoRA 82%, Full-FT 83%\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle (green shades): adaptive 75%, fixed 73.1%, feature 76.9%\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"A1 (orange): 91.5% (但标注 '99.6% fake')\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Horizontal dashed line at baseline CAR\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Secondary info: fake_safe_rate annotation above each bar\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Message: oracle CAR < baseline CAR, and all nearly 100% fake\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary: Table 3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: analysis_claim3\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    priority: must\\\\n\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  - table_id: tab1_fake_safety\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Fake safety analysis. Standard CAR appears high, but displacement-filtered CAR reveals that 96-99.6\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\% of 'safe' episodes involve action collapse (displacement < 0.1mm).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: analysis_claim1\\\\n    type: analysis\\\\n    columns: [Method, Episodes, TSR, CAR, \\\\\\\"Fake Rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"CAR_f\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary Table 2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"CAR_f = displacement-filtered CAR (proposed metric). Fake Rate = fraction of safe episodes with displacement < τ_d.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab2_pi05_a1_placeholder\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"[PLACEHOLDER] Pi0.5 + SDF auxiliary loss (3-seed × 2-lambda). Pending 30K evaluation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: analysis_claim4_placeholder\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Config, TSR, CAR, \\\\\\\"Frozen Rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"CAR_f\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"ROADMAP D016 (10K preview) + pending 30K eval\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab3_oracle\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Oracle SDF refinement with ground-truth distance fields. All three variants achieve lower CAR than unrefined baselines, and fake safe rates remain above 96\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\%.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: analysis_claim3\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Method, TSR, CAR, \\\\\\\"Fake Rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Refines/ep\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"paper_data_summary Table 3\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 30\\\\n  macro_context:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"VLA safety and collision avoidance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"signed distance fields in robot manipulation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"evaluation metric reliability in robot learning / ML\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"action collapse and mode collapse in generative policies\\\\\\\"\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"collision-aware-vla\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"collision avoidance vision language action model 2024 2025 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"safe VLA manipulation policy constraint\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"AEGIS/VLSA (Hu et al. 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SafeVLA (Zhang et al. 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"CoFreeVLA (2026)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"sdf-robotics\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"signed distance field robot collision differentiable 2021 2022 2023 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"DeepSDF (Park et al. 2019)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"DiffCo (Zhi et al. 2021)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"vla-foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"π0 (Black et al. 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OpenVLA (Kim et al. 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LIBERO (Liu et al. 2023)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"metric-reliability\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"evaluation metric reliability robot learning benchmark 2023 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"benchmark saturation gaming machine learning evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"safety metric validity robotics\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite: []\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"action-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"action collapse VLA policy mode collapse frozen 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"mode collapse diffusion policy degenerate behavior\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"action repetition failure mode learned policy\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite: []\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - analysis_claim1      # Fake Safety — core finding, sets up everything\\\\n  - analysis_claim2      # TSR-CAR anti-correlation\\\\n  - analysis_claim3      # EE-only limitation\\\\n  - experimental_framework  # Method/setup — informed by what results need\\\\n  - introduction          # Narrative wrapper\\\\n  - related_work          # Positioning\\\\n  - abstract              # Distillation\\\\n  - analysis_claim4_placeholder  # Brief placeholder\\\\n  - conclusion_placeholder       # Brief placeholder\\\\n\\\\ncolor_palette:\\\\n  baseline_pi0: \\\\\\\"#808080\\\\\\\"       # gray — Pi0 baselines (action collapsed)\\\\n  baseline_pi05: \\\\\\\"#0072B2\\\\\\\"      # blue — Pi0.5 baselines (capable but unsafe)\\\\n  a1_sdf: \\\\\\\"#E69F00\\\\\\\"             # orange — A1 SDF methods\\\\n  oracle: \\\\\\\"#009E73\\\\\\\"             # green — Oracle variants\\\\n  pi05_a1: \\\\\\\"#D55E00\\\\\\\"            # vermillion — Pi0.5+A1 (promising)\\\\n  fake_zone: \\\\\\\"#FFCCCC\\\\\\\"          # light red — fake safety zone\\\\n  real_zone: \\\\\\\"#CCFFCC\\\\\\\"          # light green — real safety zone\\\\n  threshold_line: \\\\\\\"#CC0000\\\\\\\"     # dark red — displacement threshold\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 15413, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0194HGtGfnwzoV7Zk1AQYGPU","session_id":"f420d955-7ae5-4224-93b3-f4bdf2a953a4","uuid":"6f290459-2c70-4730-98c5-915dc11fb04c","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:04:49.758Z"}
