{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015YUbr79Tzsyy5UmTPdHYRx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\section{Experimental Framework}\\label{sec:framework}\n2\t\n3\tThis section defines the evaluation platform, metrics, and model configurations that underpin the analyses in Sections~\\ref{sec:fake_safety}--\\ref{sec:a1_pi05}. Our primary methodological contribution is the displacement-filtered Collision Avoidance Rate (CAR$_\\text{f}$), which separates genuine avoidance from action collapse.\n4\t\n5\t\\subsection{Benchmark and Evaluation Protocol}\\label{sec:benchmark}\n6\t\n7\tWe conduct all experiments on SafeLIBERO~\\cite{hu2025vlsa}, a collision-aware evaluation extension of the LIBERO simulation platform~\\cite{liu2023libero}. SafeLIBERO augments standard manipulation benchmarks with per-timestep collision detection and non-target obstacle annotations, enabling systematic measurement of both task completion and safety.\n8\t\n9\tWe select the \\textit{object\\_pudding} Level~I suite, which comprises four tabletop manipulation tasks. In each task, a target object is surrounded by non-target obstacles that the robot must avoid during grasping and transport. The MuJoCo physics engine provides collision detection: any contact between the robot (end-effector or arm links) and a non-target object registers as a collision event.\n10\t\n11\tEach method is evaluated for 50 episodes per task (200 episodes total). For multi-seed experiments (Pi0.5), we run 3 seeds to produce 600 episodes per configuration. Initial object configurations are fixed across methods to ensure fair comparison.\n12\t\n13\t\\subsection{Evaluation Metrics}\\label{sec:metrics}\n14\t\n15\t\\paragraph{Standard metrics.} We report two conventional metrics. The \\emph{Task Success Rate} (TSR) is the fraction of episodes where the manipulation task reaches completion. The \\emph{Collision Avoidance Rate} (CAR) is the fraction of episodes in which no collision occurs between the robot and any non-target object.\n16\t\n17\t\\paragraph{Displacement-filtered CAR.} Standard CAR conflates two qualitatively distinct behaviors: a robot that plans a trajectory around obstacles, and a robot that has collapsed into inaction. Both register as ``safe,'' yet only the former reflects collision avoidance capability. We propose the displacement-filtered CAR (CAR$_\\text{f}$), which excludes episodes exhibiting action collapse from both numerator and denominator.\n18\t\n19\tWe define an episode $e$ as \\emph{action-collapsed} when its maximum end-effector displacement satisfies $d_{\\max}(e) < \\tau_d$, where $\\tau_d = 0.1$\\,mm. The filtered metric is then:\n20\t\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:car_f}\n21\t\\text{CAR}_\\text{f} = \\frac{|\\{e : \\text{safe}(e) \\;\\land\\; d_{\\max}(e) \\geq \\tau_d\\}|}{|\\{e : d_{\\max}(e) \\geq \\tau_d\\}|}\n22\t\\end{equation}\n23\twhere $d_{\\max}(e)$ denotes the maximum Euclidean displacement of the end-effector across all timesteps in episode $e$. The threshold $\\tau_d = 0.1$\\,mm corresponds to sub-actuator-resolution motion and is robust to perturbation (Appendix~\\ref{app:threshold_sensitivity}).\n24\t\n25\t\\paragraph{Auxiliary metrics.} We additionally report the \\emph{Frozen Rate}, the fraction of episodes with $d_{\\max} < \\tau_d$, which quantifies the severity of action collapse for each method. The \\emph{Simultaneous Success Rate} (SSR $= $ TSR $\\cap$ CAR) measures the fraction of episodes that achieve both task completion and collision avoidance.\n26\t\n27\t\\subsection{Models and Training}\\label{sec:models}\n28\t\n29\t\\paragraph{Base architectures.} We evaluate two VLA models from the Pi0 family~\\cite{black2024pi0}. \\textbf{Pi0} (${\\sim}$3B parameters) uses a PaliGemma vision-language encoder paired with a dedicated action expert that generates continuous actions via flow matching~\\cite{lipman2023flow}. \\textbf{Pi0.5} extends this architecture to ${\\sim}$3.5B parameters with broader pre-training data, and serves as a stronger baseline that exhibits less action collapse.\n30\t\n31\t\\paragraph{Training configurations.} We evaluate four model variants:\n32\t\\begin{itemize}\n33\t\\item \\textit{Full-FT baseline}: Pi0 with all parameters fine-tuned on SafeLIBERO demonstrations using the flow-matching action loss.\n34\t\\item \\textit{LoRA baseline}: Pi0 with LoRA adapters (${\\sim}$33.5M trainable parameters), same demonstrations and loss.\n35\t\\item \\textit{A1-LoRA}: Pi0 + LoRA augmented with two auxiliary heads. An SDF Decoder (4-layer MLP, ${\\sim}$395K parameters) predicts the signed distance from the end-effector to the nearest obstacle surface, supervised with a clamped $L_1$ loss and an Eikonal regularizer ($\\mathcal{L}_\\text{SDF}$). An EE Extractor (2-layer MLP, ${\\sim}$263K parameters) predicts end-effector position from action expert features ($\\mathcal{L}_\\text{EE}$, MSE loss). SDF ground truth is computed from known obstacle meshes in simulation.\n36\t\\item \\textit{Pi0.5 + A1}: The A1 architecture applied to the Pi0.5 backbone. Training proceeds in two phases: Phase~1 (steps 0--5K) trains only the auxiliary heads on detached features with the backbone frozen; Phase~2 (steps 5K--30K) unfreezes LoRA parameters for joint optimization. We evaluate $\\lambda_\\text{SDF} \\in \\{0.005, 0.01\\}$.\n37\t\\end{itemize}\n38\t\n39\t\\subsection{Oracle SDF Refinement}\\label{sec:oracle_setup}\n40\t\n41\tTo test the theoretical upper bound of end-effector-only SDF refinement (analyzed in Section~\\ref{sec:ee_only}), we replace the learned SDF network with the ground-truth signed distance field computed from simulation geometry. This eliminates prediction error and isolates the structural limitation of the refinement paradigm itself.\n42\t\n43\tWe evaluate three oracle variants that differ in how the SDF gradient is applied:\n44\t\\begin{itemize}\n45\t\\item \\textit{Oracle-adaptive}: runtime gradient refinement with a dynamic step size $\\alpha$ that scales inversely with gradient magnitude.\n46\t\\item \\textit{Oracle-fixed}: a constant step size $\\alpha = 0.005$.\n47\t\\item \\textit{Oracle-feature}: gradient applied in the VLA's latent feature space rather than Cartesian action space.\n48\t\\end{itemize}\n49\tEach variant is evaluated for 160 episodes (4 tasks $\\times$ 40 episodes) with a single seed.\n50\t\n51\t\\subsection{SDF Ground Truth}\\label{sec:sdf_gt}\n52\t\n53\tThe workspace signed distance field is computed from the known obstacle meshes available in the LIBERO/MuJoCo simulation environment. SDF values are positive in free space, zero on the obstacle surface, and negative inside the obstacle volume. Ground-truth labels are generated at query points sampled along predicted end-effector trajectories during training.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0194HGtGfnwzoV7Zk1AQYGPU","session_id":"f420d955-7ae5-4224-93b3-f4bdf2a953a4","uuid":"b862a28e-da0a-4def-a467-cba3dd42581b","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:05:09.337Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016NBEhasjBmF646ebkE5Q76","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/diff_collision_sdf/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# diff_collision_sdf — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-25 22:31 UTC | 更新原因: MVP 通过, 进入 Research 阶段, D023 修正叙事, post-MVP kickoff Steps 1-4 完成\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-26 ~06:00 UTC | 更新原因: MVP 通过 (D023), 进入 Research 阶段, \\\\\\\"30K collapse\\\\\\\" 叙事被推翻\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\nVLA safety 评估方法论缺陷：CAR 被 action collapse / geometric path safety 污染，98%+ 的表面安全是假象。提出 EE displacement-filtered CAR + SDF auxiliary loss 作为验证工具。详见 `paper_framing.md`。\\\\n\\\\n## 当前进展\\\\n- **阶段**: Research（MVP 2026-05-26 通过）\\\\n- **目标**: CoRL 2026 Main / ICRA 2027\\\\n- **核心发现**: SDF 产生真实碰撞避免（EE ~0.5m, 0% fake, +25pp CAR），但 tradeoff 极端（TSR -65pp）。效果跨步数稳定（D023 推翻 \\\\\\\"30K collapse\\\\\\\"）\\\\n- **Claims**: 1★★★★★ 2★★★ 3★★★★ 4★★★★ — Claim 4 强度待 LoRA baseline 归因\\\\n- **Dream**: dream_20260525T223036 pending (full review mode)\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [x] MVP 通过 (complete_mvp)\\\\n- [x] paper_framing.md 更新 (D023 修正)\\\\n- [x] experiment_plan.yaml 创建 (11 experiments, P0×6 + P1×5)\\\\n- [x] dream_simulate 启动\\\\n- [ ] 等 Dream 回调 → 按指令处理\\\\n- [ ] LoRA baseline 完成 (ETA ~09:30 UTC) → eval → Claim 4 归因决定\\\\n- [ ] Phase 2 λ=0 完成 → eval → 是否升级 solution paper\\\\n- [ ] A1 EE disp re-eval → Claim 1 术语验证\\\\n- [ ] OpenVLA eval → Claim 1 跨模型泛化\\\\n- [ ] spatial_bowl 训练完成 (~24h) → eval → Claim 4 跨场景\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 分配\\\\n| 服务器 | GPU | 实验 | ETA |\\\\n|--------|-----|------|-----|\\\\n| westd-35807 | 0 | spatial_bowl 训练 (38%) | ~May 27 06:00 |\\\\n| westd-35807 | 1 | A1 EE disp re-eval | ~45min (启动中) |\\\\n| westd-35807 | 2 | OpenVLA / lambda 实验 | TBD |\\\\n| westd-35807 | 3 | Phase 2 λ=0 seed2 训练 | ~20h |\\\\n| westd-45947 | 0 | LoRA baseline s0 (step 26K/30K) | ~09:30 UTC |\\\\n| westd-45947 | 1 | LoRA baseline s1 (step 26K/30K) | ~09:30 UTC |\\\\n\\\\n**利用率**: 5-6/6（GPU 1/2 有短期任务或待分配）\\\\n\\\\n## 关键时间线\\\\n| 时间 | 事件 | 行动 |\\\\n|------|------|------|\\\\n| +45min | A1 re-eval 完成 | 确认 Claim 1 EE disp |\\\\n| +3-4h | LoRA baseline 完成 | 立即 eval, 决定 Claim 4 归因 |\\\\n| +20h | Phase 2 λ=0 完成 | eval, 判断是否升级 paper |\\\\n| +24h | spatial_bowl 完成 | eval 跨场景泛化 |\\\\n| Dream 回调 | dream 完成 | 审查 framing/plan 调整 |\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n- 已分配: 6 GPU (westd-35807 × 4 + westd-45947 × 2)\\\\n- P0 实验剩余 GPU-hours: ~60h (LoRA eval 20h + Phase 2 eval 10h + OpenVLA 5h + etc)\\\\n- P1 实验 GPU-hours: ~98h (spatial eval + lambda=0.1 + full A1 re-eval)\\\\n- 按 6 GPU 计, P0+P1 全部完成需 ~3 天\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D023 | 2026-05-25 | D023: \\\\\\\"30K action collapse\\\\\\\"叙事被修正数据彻底推翻——30K EE dis | eval_pi05_a1_30k_s0_l005_r4, eval_pi05_a1_best_s2_l005_10k, eval_pi05_a1_best_s1_l005_16k, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s1_l005_disp |\\\\n| D022 | 2026-05-25 | D022: 暂停\\\\\\\"30K = action collapse / 100% frozen\\\\\\\"叙事——旧 | eval_pi05_a1_30k_s1_l005_disp, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s0_l005_r4, eval_pi05_a1_best_s2_l005_10k, eval_pi05_a1_best_s1_l005_16k |\\\\n| D021 | 2026-05-25 | D021: Displacement 度量修复方案——用 EE displacement 替代 ob | eval_pi05_a1_30k_s1_l005, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s2_l005, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s1_l01, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s2_l01 |\\\\n| D020 | 2026-05-25 | D020: 30K TSR退化揭示safety-performance tradeoff——10K是 | eval_pi05_a1_30k_s1_l005, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s1_l01, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s2_l005, eval_pi05_a1_30k_s2_l01 |\\\\n| D019 | 2026-05-25 | D019: 16 个阴性结果叙事分层——Tier A (核心贡献, 正文讨论) / Tier B ( | a1_sdf_object_pudding_s0, oracle_true_gt_adaptive_alpha_v11, oracle_true_gt_fixed_alpha_v11, oracle_true_gt_feature_object_v11, train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l005, train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l01 |\\\\n| D018 | 2026-05-24 | D018: 16 个阴性结果系统分析确认方法边界——gradient-based action co | oracle_true_gt_adaptive_alpha_v11, oracle_true_gt_fixed_alpha_v11, oracle_true_gt_feature