{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0194HGtGfnwzoV7Zk1AQYGPU","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is a summary of the key findings:\n\n**Overall: 6/10 (borderline accept) at Confidence 4/5.**\n\n**Core assessment:** The diagnostic contribution (fake safety finding, dfCAR metric) is strong and well-evidenced across 6000+ episodes and 3 model families. The constructive contribution (SDF auxiliary loss + two-phase training) has meaningful statistical gaps that must be addressed.\n\n**Critical weaknesses identified:**\n\n1. **Phase 2 single seed** -- The paper's most important constructive result (TSR=48%, CAR=45%) rests on 1 seed. This needs at minimum 2 additional seeds.\n\n2. **OpenVLA asymmetry** -- Zero-shot evaluation confounds \"fake safety is architecture-general\" with \"OOD models freeze.\" Fine-tuning or proper scoping is needed.\n\n3. **EE-only paradox unresolved** -- The paper establishes EE-only SDF refinement fails structurally (Claim 3) then uses EE-only SDF supervision successfully (Claim 4) without reconciling the two.\n\n4. **Displacement threshold confusion** -- 0.1mm (action collapse) vs 0.1m (dfCAR) needs clear disambiguation.\n\n5. **No evaluation of published safety methods** -- Applying dfCAR to AEGIS/SafeVLA would transform the finding from self-diagnosis to field-wide impact.\n\n**Path to acceptance (7-8):** Replicate Phase 2 across 3 seeds, properly scope OpenVLA, and ideally apply dfCAR to at least one published safety method.\n\nReport saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/diff_collision_sdf/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260525T223036/best/review_report.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: abde44fdf9b553c83 (use SendMessage with to: 'abde44fdf9b553c83' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 100191\ntool_uses: 31\nduration_ms: 183695</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f420d955-7ae5-4224-93b3-f4bdf2a953a4","uuid":"ac979206-75a9-4114-bfff-7dc0a7aa1c54","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:07:34.665Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a robotics/ML conference review (CoRL). Your focus areas are **Methods** and **Experiments**. \n\n## Venue Standards\nCoRL (Conference on Robot Learning). Acceptance rate ~36%. OpenReview 1-10 scale:\n- 10: Top 5%, seminal\n- 9: Top 15%, strong accept  \n- 8: Top 50%, clear accept\n- 7: Good paper, accept\n- 6: Marginally above threshold\n- 5: Marginally below threshold\n- 4: Not good enough, reject\n- 3: Clear rejection\n\nReview dimensions: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations.\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation: When 98% of Collision Avoidance is an Illusion\"\n\nThe paper studies Vision-Language-Action (VLA) model safety evaluation. Key claims:\n\n1. **Fake safety taxonomy**: The widely-used Collision Avoidance Rate (CAR) metric is systematically contaminated by two failure modes—action collapse (robot freezes, trivially safe) and geometric path safety (conservative motions that coincidentally avoid obstacles). Across Pi0 (170M), Pi0.5 (300M), and OpenVLA (7B), 92–99.6% of \"safe\" episodes are fake.\n\n2. **Displacement-filtered CAR (dfCAR)**: Proposed corrected metric: dfCAR = |{i: d_obs_i < ε ∧ d_ee_i > δ}| / N, using δ=0.1m threshold based on minimum displacement to complete SafeLIBERO tasks.\n\n3. **SDF auxiliary loss**: Training-time Signed Distance Field loss on Pi0.5 via LoRA produces real collision avoidance (+25pp filtered CAR, 0% fake safety), but devastates task performance (TSR: 73%→7%). 4-point λ curve shows dose-dependent relationship.\n\n4. **Two-phase training**: SDF pre-training (10K steps, λ=0.005) → standard fine-tuning (20K steps, λ=0) recovers TSR to 48% while retaining 81% safety encoding (CAR 45%, fake safe 5%).\n\n**Key experimental results** (from paper Tables 1-10):\n- Table 1: A1 (Pi0+LoRA+SDF) action collapse confirmed: 800ep obstacle disp median ~5nm, 50ep EE disp 96% < 1mm\n- Table 2: Cross-model comparison: Pi0 A1 (CAR 91.5%, fake 99.6%), Pi0.5 baseline (CAR 26.8%, fake 98.2%), OpenVLA (CAR 88%, fake 92%)\n- Table 3: OpenVLA per-task (4 tasks, 200ep total)\n- Table 4: LoRA attribution - LoRA-only CAR=27±1.4% ≈ zero-shot 26.8±1.6%, confirming SDF is the driver\n- Table 5: Per-task LoRA vs SDF showing asymmetry (milk +70pp, bbq_sauce -24pp)\n- Table 6: 4-point λ curve: λ∈{0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.1}, CAR monotonically increasing with diminishing returns\n- Table 7: Two-phase results: TSR=48%, CAR=45%, fake safe=5%\n- Table 8: Per-task Phase 2 breakdown, 76-100% safety retention\n- Table 9: Cross-scene (object_pudding vs spatial_bowl), both show +25-32pp CAR\n- Table 10: spatial_bowl per-task results\n\n**Experimental scale**: 70+ experiments, 6000+ episodes, 3 model families, 2 scenes, multiple seeds.\n\n## Experiment Design Context (from review_context.yaml)\nThe paper's imagined experiments include:\n- A1 EE Displacement Re-eval (50ep) — validates action collapse via EE metric\n- OpenVLA Zero-shot SafeLIBERO Eval (200ep) — cross-architecture validation\n- LoRA Baseline Eval (2 seeds) — attribution control\n- Phase 2 λ=0 Ablation Training (10K→30K) — two-phase strategy\n- Phase 2 λ=0 Eval (200ep) — key results\n- spatial_bowl A1 Eval (200ep) — cross-scene\n- Lambda=0.1 Bracket Training + Eval — dose-response curve\n\nNotable: The paper covers all planned experiments from the design. OpenVLA is zero-shot only (no fine-tuning). Phase 2 has only 1 seed. spatial_bowl has only 1 seed.\n\n## Your Task\nWrite a detailed review focusing on:\n\n### Methods Evaluation\n- Is dfCAR well-motivated and well-defined? Is δ=0.1m justified?\n- Is the SDF loss formulation sound? Any issues with EE-only supervision?\n- Is the two-phase training protocol well-designed? Are the phase durations justified?\n- Are there methodological gaps or confounds?\n\n### Experiments Evaluation  \n- Are experiments sufficient to support each claim?\n- Statistical rigor: seed counts, episode counts, confidence intervals\n- Are baselines adequate? Missing comparisons?\n- Cross-architecture claim (3 models) — is OpenVLA zero-shot a fair comparison?\n- Cross-scene claim (2 scenes) — sufficient for generalization?\n- Phase 2 single seed — is this a concern?\n- Any cherry-picking risks?\n\n### Output Format\nProvide your review in this structure:\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods & Experiments\n\n### Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths (bulleted)\n\n### Weaknesses (bulleted)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n\n### Missing Experiments or Controls\n\n### Scoring\n- Quality: X/10\n- Clarity: X/10\n- Significance: X/10\n- Relevance: X/10\n- Overall: X/10\n- Confidence: X/5 (1=low, 5=expert)\n```\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a CoRL-level review.\n","agentId":"abde44fdf9b553c83","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is a summary of the key findings:\n\n**Overall: 6/10 (borderline accept) at Confidence 4/5.**\n\n**Core assessment:** The diagnostic contribution (fake safety finding, dfCAR metric) is strong and well-evidenced across 6000+ episodes and 3 model families. The constructive contribution (SDF auxiliary loss + two-phase training) has meaningful statistical gaps that must be addressed.\n\n**Critical weaknesses identified:**\n\n1. **Phase 2 single seed** -- The paper's most important constructive result (TSR=48%, CAR=45%) rests on 1 seed. This needs at minimum 2 additional seeds.\n\n2. **OpenVLA asymmetry** -- Zero-shot evaluation confounds \"fake safety is architecture-general\" with \"OOD models freeze.\" Fine-tuning or proper scoping is needed.\n\n3. **EE-only paradox unresolved** -- The paper establishes EE-only SDF refinement fails structurally (Claim 3) then uses EE-only SDF supervision successfully (Claim 4) without reconciling the two.\n\n4. **Displacement threshold confusion** -- 0.1mm (action collapse) vs 0.1m (dfCAR) needs clear disambiguation.\n\n5. **No evaluation of published safety methods** -- Applying dfCAR to AEGIS/SafeVLA would transform the finding from self-diagnosis to field-wide impact.\n\n**Path to acceptance (7-8):** Replicate Phase 2 across 3 seeds, properly scope OpenVLA, and ideally apply dfCAR to at least one published safety method.\n\nReport saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/diff_collision_sdf/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260525T223036/best/review_report.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":183695,"totalTokens":100191,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4040,"cache_read_input_tokens":95716,"output_tokens":434,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4040},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":95716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4040,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4040,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":11,"searchCount":5,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":15}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013G2BZSPirMsaTDhS98JKyz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have both R1 and R2 reviews. Now I need to do the full roundtable process:\n\n- Step 1: Independent reviews (done - R1 and R2 have submitted)\n- Step 2: Cross-sharing (I share each reviewer's findings with the other)\n- Step 3: Convergence (identify agreements/disagreements, reconcile)\n- Step 4: Synthesis (final consolidated review report)\n\nLet me first capture the key points from both reviews, then do the roundtable steps.\n\n**R1 Summary:**\n- Overall: 6/10 (borderline accept), Confidence 4/5\n\n\n- Strengths: Strong diagnostic contribution, thorough experiments (6000+ episodes), dfCAR well-motivated\n- Key weaknesses: Phase 2 single seed, OpenVLA zero-shot asymmetry confusion, unresolved EE-only paradox, displacement threshold inconsistency (0.1mm vs 0.1m), and no evaluation of published safety methods with dfCAR\n\n**R2 Summary:**\n- Overall: 5/10 (marginally below), Confidence 4/5\n- Strengths: Compelling empirical observation, thorough methodology, two-phase result interesting\n- Additional concerns: Fake safety observation lacks conceptual novelty, dfCAR itself is minimal, SDF auxiliary loss combines existing techniques without clear innovation, two-phase approach not positioned against curriculum learning, safety-performance tradeoff severely underexplored, only 5 references cited, and scope limited to SafeLIBERO alone\n\nNow I'm moving through the roundtable process—identifying where reviewers converge and diverge, reconciling differences, and synthesizing into a final report. Both reviewers recognize the diagnostic value, so I'll build the synthesis from there. contribution as the paper's primary strength\n- Both flag Phase 2 single seed as a serious concern\n- Both note OpenVLA zero-shot is problematic for the generalization claim\n- Both give high relevance scores (8/10)\n- Both note the paper is well-written\n\nKey disagreements:\n- R1 gives 6/10 overall (borderline accept), R2 gives 5/10 (marginally below)\n- R1 is more positive about dfCAR as a contribution; R2 considers it trivial\n- R2 is much more critical about novelty and related work (only 5 references)\n- R2 raises the curriculum learning connection that R1 doesn't mention\n\nConvergence:\n- The novelty concern from R2 is legitimate — the observation is important but conceptually simple\n- The 5-reference issue is severe for any top venue\n- Phase 2 single seed is a consensus weakness\n- Reframing this as a diagnostic study with quantification rather than a novel method makes more sense, and the consensus score should land somewhere between 5 and 6\n\nNow I'll put together the final synthesis report.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7296,"cache_read_input_tokens":59819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7296},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f420d955-7ae5-4224-93b3-f4bdf2a953a4","uuid":"c4f6adda-6aed-4b3c-8b0b-2196cee79b63"}
